UNIT f64_canonical_bits
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 3c0b7f98393070d57862813cef57df44b98940a1fb81567dc0cc6f17c633512d
SIG export function f64_canonical_bits(raw: string): string
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime: text=string; result string. STRICT: the artifact must type-check under
  `strict: true` against this SIG, with no `any`, no non-null assertions (`!`), and no `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`.
  BigInt literals and DataView.setBigUint64/getBigUint64 need a target of ES2020 or later.
MECHANISM (restated from js — language files are self-contained) R1 = the HEX16 pin tested over the whole string (no m
  flag, so $ matches only at the very end and a trailing line feed fails), throw an Error otherwise. R2 = BigInt('0x' + raw)
  written with DataView.setBigUint64 (big-endian), read back with getFloat64. R3 = Number.isNaN on that number returns QNAN
  without consulting any bits: the engine may canonicalize or preserve a NaN payload through DataView, so the payload must
  never be what decides. R4 = setFloat64 then getBigUint64, rendered with toString(16) and left-padded with '0' to 16 digits.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex HEX16 = /^[0-9a-f]{16}$/ CITED R1 — no i flag, no m flag
PROVENANCE rederive@b15b56613f9d cli/sir/canon.mjs lines 8-13.
